## Boundary rules

- Add behavior to the module that owns the responsibility and data.
- Communicate across modules through an existing public contract where one
  exists; do not import another module's internals.
- Do not create a dependency cycle or a convenience dependency that reverses
  the approved direction.
- Keep side effects behind explicit boundaries so core logic remains testable.
- A new cross-module dependency, public entrypoint, or shared module triggers
  `docs/CHANGE_IMPACT.md` and renewed approval when absent from the task plan.

